\begin{abstract}
Recent advances in deep learning have spurred the development of end-to-end frameworks for portfolio optimization that utilize implicit layers. However, many such implementations are highly sensitive to neural network initialization, undermining performance consistency. This research introduces a robust end-to-end framework tailored for risk budgeting portfolios that effectively reduces sensitivity to initialization. Importantly, this enhanced stability does not compromise portfolio performance, as our framework consistently outperforms the risk parity benchmark.
\end{abstract}

%In conclusion, the End-to-End framework represents a significant advancement in the field of portfolio optimization, offering a comprehensive approach that integrates traditional financial principles with modern machine learning techniques. However, the successful implementation of this framework hinges on the establishment of smooth connections among its layers and the ability to generalize to various investment objectives. Our proposed extension, featuring a bounded softmax layer, addresses these challenges by enhancing numerical stability and enabling the framework to accommodate a larger set of assets. Through our case study on mean-variance and risk budgeting optimization, we demonstrate the practical benefits of this extension, paving the way for more robust and adaptable portfolio optimization strategies. As the financial landscape continues to evolve, the insights gained from our research will be invaluable for investors seeking to leverage advanced methodologies in their pursuit of optimal portfolio performance.


Keywords: end-to-end framework, neural networks, risk budgeting, stability\\

