\begin{thm} Let $\pi: M(c) \rightarrow N$ be an anti-invariant submersion from a quaternionic space form $\left(M(c), g_M\right)$ onto a Riemannian manifold  $(N, g_N).$  Then we have
\begin{equation}\label{eq-3.57}
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{c}{4}\left((\ell+r)(\ell+r-1)+\sum_{\alpha =1}^{3}\left( \sum_{i=1}^{\ell} 6\lVert B_{J_\alpha}X_i \rVert ^{2}+3 \lVert C_{J_\alpha}X_{1} \rVert ^{2}\right) \right) \geq \\
&  \hat{\tau}+ \tau^*+r^2\|H\|^2-\left\|{\mathcal{T}}^{\mathcal{H}}\right\|^2-2 \delta(N)-2\left\|{\mathcal{A}}^{\mathcal{H}}\right\|^2+2 \sqrt{6}\left\|{\mathcal{A}}^{\mathcal{V}}\right\|\left\|{\mathcal{T}}^{\mathcal{V}}\right\|.
