 Finally, we easily check that $f^3$ is not a $D$-coboundary. Thus it is the generating class of $Ext_{(\Lambda V,d)}(\mathbb{Q},(\Lambda V,d))$.
 Hence, $t= 3$ so that $L_0 = t-1 =2$. Moreover, in $(\Lambda V,d)$, we have $[f^t(1)] = [f(1)] = [x_4^2] = [x_2^4]$,  hence, by definition of $e_0(\Lambda V,d)$, we in fact obtain: 
