\begin{section}{Numerical simulations of the 2-mSP equation and the CmSP equation}
\label{sec_numexpMCmSP}

In this section, we construct self-adaptive moving mesh schemes of the 2-mSP equation and the CmSP equation.

The 2-mSP equation
\begin{eqnarray}
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
u_{xt}=u+\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}v(u^{2})_{xx}, \\
\\
v_{xt}=v+\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}u(v^{2})_{xx},
\end{array}
\right.
\label{2mSP}
\end{eqnarray}
is a special case of the MCmSP equation (\ref{MCmSP}) with $n=2, u^{(1)}=u, u^{(2)}=v$ and $c_{12}=1$.

Based on the results in the previous section, we have a self-adaptive moving mesh scheme for the 2-mSP equation
\begin{eqnarray}
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\displaystyle\frac{d }{d T}(u_{l+1}-u_{l})=(\delta_{l}-a)(u_{l+1}+u_{l}), \\
\\
\displaystyle\frac{d}{d T}(v_{l+1}-v_{l})=(\delta_{l}-a)(v_{l+1}+v_{l}),\\
\\
\displaystyle\frac{d x_{l}}{d T}=-u_{l}v_{l}.
\end{array}
\right.
\label{semidis2mSP}
\end{eqnarray}
Here, $u_{l}$ and $v_{l}$ are values at $x_{l}$.

Equation (\ref{semidis2mSP}) admits the following N-soliton solution
\begin{eqnarray}
u_{l}=\frac{g_{l}^{(1)}}{f_{l}},\qquad v_{l}=\frac{g_{l}^{(2)}}{f_{l}}, \qquad x_{l}=2la-(\log{f_{l}})_{T},\qquad t=T,
\end{eqnarray}
with
\begin{eqnarray}
\fl{f_{l}={\rm Pf}(a_{1},\cdots,a_{2N},b_{1},\cdots,b_{2N})_{l}, \qquad
g^{(i)}_{l}={\rm Pf}(d_{0},B_{i},a_{1},\cdots,a_{2N},b_{1},\cdots,b_{2N})_{l},}
\end{eqnarray}
where $i=1,2$ and the elements of the Pfaffians are defined as (\ref{dmpf1})-(\ref{dmpf2}).

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
% 2mSP 初期条件
%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%

Here we show examples of numerical simulations of the 2-mSP equation  (\ref{2mSP}) with a self-adaptive moving mesh scheme (\ref{semidis2mSP}) under the periodic boundary condition. The initial conditions are given by
\begin{eqnarray}
u=\frac{g^{(1)}}{f},\quad v=\frac{g^{(2)}}{f},\quad x=X-(\log{f})_{T},\quad t=T,\nonumber\\
f=-1-a_{1}a_{2}b_{12}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{2}},\qquad g^{(1)}=-a_{1}e^{\eta_{1}}, \qquad g^{(2)}=-a_{2}e^{\eta_{2}},\nonumber\\
\eta_{i}=p_{i}X+\frac{1}{p_{i}}T+\xi_{i}^{\prime},\quad b_{ij}=\left(\frac{p_{i}p_{j}}{p_{i}+p_{j}}\right)^{2},\quad i,j=1,2,\label{incon_mSP_1}
\end{eqnarray}
and
\begin{eqnarray}
u=\frac{g^{(1)}}{f},\quad v=\frac{g^{(2)}}{f},\quad x=X-(\log{f})_{T},\quad t=T, \nonumber\\
\fl{f=1+a_{1}a_{3}b_{13}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{3}}+a_{2}a_{3}b_{23}e^{\eta_{2}+\eta_{3}}+a_{1}a_{4}b_{14}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{4}}+a_{2}a_{4}b_{24}e^{\eta_{2}+\eta_{4}}}\nonumber\\
\fl{\qquad+a_{1}a_{2}a_{3}a_{4}(p_{1}-p_{2})^{2}(p_{3}-p_{4})^{2}\frac{b_{13}b_{23}b_{14}b_{24}}{p_{1}^{2}p_{2}^{2}p_{3}^{2}p_{4}^{2}}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{2}+\eta_{3}+\eta_{4}},}\nonumber\\
\fl{g^{(1)}=a_{1}e^{\eta_{1}}+a_{2}e^{\eta_{2}}+\frac{a_{1}a_{2}a_{3}(p_{1}-p_{2})^{2}p_{3}^{4}}{(p_{1}+p_{3})^{2}(p_{2}+p_{3})^{2}}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{2}+\eta_{3}}+\frac{a_{1}a_{2}a_{4}(p_{1}-p_{2})^{2}p_{4}^{4}}{(p_{1}+p_{4})^{2}(p_{2}+p_{4})^{2}}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{2}+\eta_{4}},}\nonumber\\
\fl{g^{(2)}=a_{3}e^{\eta_{3}}+a_{4}e^{\eta_{4}}+\frac{a_{2}a_{3}a_{4}(p_{3}-p_{4})^{2}p_{2}^{4}}{(p_{2}+p_{3})^{2}(p_{2}+p_{4})^{2}}e^{\eta_{2}+\eta_{3}+\eta_{4}}+\frac{a_{1}a_{3}a_{4}(p_{3}-p_{4})^{2}p_{1}^{4}}{(p_{1}+p_{3})^{2}(p_{1}+p_{4})^{2}}e^{\eta_{1}+\eta_{3}+\eta_{4}},}\nonumber\\
\eta_{i}=p_{i}X+\frac{1}{p_{i}}T+\xi_{i}^{\prime},\quad b_{ij}=\left(\frac{p_{i}p_{j}}{p_{i}+p_{j}}\right)^{2},\quad i,j=1,2,3,4,\label{incon_mSP_2}
\end{eqnarray}
which are exact one- and two-soliton solutions of the 2-mSP equation obtained in Example 2.3.

As a time marching method, we use the improved Euler method.
The mesh grid points are $n=8000,$ the width of the computational domain is  $D=80$, and the time interval is $dt=0.0001$.

