\(B\)-detection occurs on \(\Omega_{\mathcal{B}}:=\mathcal{B}\times\Omega\ni\omega_B:=(B,\omega)%\in\Omega_\mathcal{B}
\) under its natural measure \({\pi}^{B}_0\times Q_B(\cdot)\) %: at any \(n\in\mathbb{N}\), for any \(\), given data \(D^n(\omega)\in\mathbf{V}^n\) and %the \(B\)-labelled laws \(Q_B\) and 
given \emph{a priori} belief \({\pi}^{B%\{B(\omega_B)=\cdot\}
}_0\). % in \(\{B(\omega_B)=\cdot\in\mathcal{B}\}\) is the \begin{equation}\label{thetaQB}d\big({\pi}^B_0Q_B(\omega_B)\big)|_{n}:={\pi}^{B(\omega_B)}_0d Q_{B(\omega_B)}|_{n}\big({D}^n(\omega)).\end{equation}
Any LR level \(L^{b\overline{b}}_n\in(0,\infty)\) maps to an inferential belief level \({\pi}^b_n\in(0,1)\): in terms of \emph{odds-for-}\(\{B=b\}\), \(O[{\pi}^b_n]:={\pi}^b_n/{\pi}^{\overline{b}}_n%\in(0,\infty)
\)%\(O[{\pi}^b_0]%\in(0,\infty)
,\begin{equation}\label{br1}
    O[{\pi}^b_n]= O[{\pi}^b_0]\cdot %\propto
    {L^{b\overline{b}}_n}%=O[{\pi}^b_0]\cdot\exp[{l^{b\overline{b}}_n}]
    =O[{\pi}^b_m]\cdot %\propto
    {L^{b\overline{b}}_{n|m}}.
    \end{equation}This correspondence is bijective and smooth; it is a version of the Bayes' Rule.

