In Fig.~\ref{fig1}, we present the constraint results on the one-dimensional (1D) marginalized posterior distributions of $w_{\rm dm}$ for the $\Lambda$nCDM model, using the current observational data. The constraint values of $w_{\rm dm}$ are $0.00084\pm 0.00035$ (CMB+DESI), $0.00059\pm 0.00033$ (CMB+DESI+DESY5), and $0.00074\pm 0.00034$ (CMB+DESI+PantheonPlus), indicating a preference for a non-zero DM EoS parameter at $2.4\sigma$, $1.8\sigma$, and $2.2\sigma$ confidence levels, respectively. Note that constraints on $\Lambda$nCDM have been presented in Ref.~\cite{Kumar:2025etf} using current cosmological data, and these results are largely consistent with ours. However, due to the differences in the CMB data and the inclusion of the PR4 lensing data in our analysis, the constraint results are slightly improved, and a slightly higher deviation is also observed.




