\begin{definition}
The \emph{Voronoi cells} with respect to $\kappa$ are tiles (with markers) in tiling $\mathcal{VC}(\kappa, \alpha)$ for some slope $\alpha$ (see Figure~\ref{fig:Voronoi-cells}).
A Voronoi cell is
\begin{itemize}
\item
\emph{small} if it is a rhombus with side length $C\kappa$, and we denote by $S = S(\kappa)$.
\item
\emph{medium} if it is a parallelogram with  side lengths $C\kappa$ and $C(\kappa + 1)$, and we denote by $M = M(\kappa)$.
\item
\emph{large} if it is a rhombus with side length $C(\kappa + 1)$, and we denote by $L = L(\kappa)$.
\end{itemize}
Each cell inherits 
the pattern from lattice $\SL(\kappa, \alpha)$ as the marker.
We call it the \emph{Sturmian Ammann bars} (abbreviated as SABs).
\end{definition}

