%In this example, we may choose $\kappa$ arbitrarily.
Since $u = 2$ and $v = -1$, we obtain
\[
\varphi(S) : \varphi(M) : \varphi(L) =
-1 : 0 : 2.
\]
One can calculate easily our target $\AA = \{2S + L, M\}$ in the proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:Voronoi-aperiodic}(2).
As long as $\TVC(\alpha)\in \TA$, we may take another tile set in $\AA(\alpha)$ such as $\{6S + 6M + 3L, M\}$.
Indeed, we realize a tile set as in Figure~\ref{fig:ex1-tiles}, consisting of three tiles up to reflection.
We prepare two kinds of patch-tiles for $6S + 6M + 3L$ as Remark~\ref{rem:upper-bound}.
See also Figure~\ref{fig:ex1-tiling} for a tiling, here a cyan tile (\textcolor{cyan!40!white}{$\blacksquare$}) is the reverse of magenta one (\textcolor{magenta!40!white}{$\blacksquare$}).
