We also give another remark, related to Remark~\ref{rem:upper-bound}.
If we aim at finding a new aperiodic monotile, then 
it might be better to set $\kappa = \infty$.
Theorem~\ref{thm:Voronoi-aperiodic} says that we must prepare at least two tiles to realize a Sturmian lattice with quadratic slope $\alpha$.
If we take $\kappa = \infty$, then there are no differences between supports of each cell, and we may reduce the number of prototiles to one, up to their color.
\subsection{Generalization of Smith Turtle}
\label{sec:ex4}

In \cite[Section~6]{SMKGS:23_1}, they propose a parameter family of 
aperiodic monotiles by varying the ratio of two edges lengths.
We remark that we can add another parameter, but the number of prototiles increases.

Recall that we did not use $\kappa_{0}$ for discussion on natural densities or BD correspondences, so changing the value of $\kappa_{0}$ does not affect the
resulting tilings.
By taking Voronoi sub-cells, we may also change $\kappa:= \kappa_{-1}$ 
(we usually use the symbol $\kappa$ without subscripts for level $0$, but in this section we use it for level $-1$ since we are mainly interested in the Voronoi sub-cells).

When we change $\kappa = \infty$ to $\kappa'\in [1, \infty)$ for the original Voronoi sub-cells, we lengthen 
sides orthogonal to SAB from 
$2/3$ to $2(\kappa' + 1) / 3\kappa'$, which has ratio
\[
\frac{2}{3} : \frac{2(\kappa' + 1)}{3\kappa'} =
\kappa' : (\kappa' + 1).
\]
We call this operation the ``SAB thickening'' and resulting the union of rectangle domains the \emph{Sturmian Ammann strips}.
See also Figure~\ref{fig:ex4-degenerated-Voronoi}(a).

The SAB thickening seems to be possible for $\kappa'\in (0, 1)$, and let us explain that the carry occurs in this case.
When we write 
\[
\frac{1}{\kappa'} = n + \frac{1}{\kappa''}
\]
with $n\in \N$ and $\kappa''\in (1, \infty]$, one can calculate $\kappa_{0}'$ with $ (\kappa_{0}', \alpha_{0}) = \sigma(\kappa', \alpha)$ as
\[
\kappa_{0}' = a_{0} + \frac{1}{\kappa'} =
(a_{0} + n) + \frac{1}{\kappa''}
\]
where $a_{0} = \floor{\alpha^{-1}}$.

This means that the SAB thickening changes parameter $\kappa_{0}$ into $\kappa_{0}'\ge \kappa_{0}$ on level~$0$.
The width of Sturmian Ammann strip 
is calculated as
\[
\frac{2(\kappa'+1)}{3\kappa'} -
\frac{2}{3} =
\frac{2}{3\kappa'} =
\frac{2}{3}(\kappa_{0}' - a_{0}) =
\frac{2}{3}(\kappa_{0}' - \kappa_{0})
\]
since $\kappa_{0} = a_{0} + 1/\kappa_{-1} = a_{0} + 1/\infty = a_{0}$
Thus, the corridor width after thickening is equal to $\kappa_{0} + (\kappa_{0}' - \kappa_{0}) = \kappa_{0}'$ as in Figure~\ref{fig:ex4-kappa}, which is consistent with the definition of $\kappa$ as a corridor width.

