\subsubsection{Inhomogeneous damage propagation in a rubber-like material}\label{sec:NonHomogeneousDamage}
%
In this example, we consider inhomogeneous damage propagation in a plane strain rubber-like material subjected to various boundary conditions. Specifically, we consider two scenarios:
%
\begin{itemize}
    \item Scenario 1: We consider a fixed rectangular geometry with prescribed damage along the left and top sides. Specifically, the damage, $d$, is ramped linearly from 0 to 0.95 over 100 seconds, then remains fixed for another 200 seconds, allowing its propagation over a total of 300 seconds, as seen in Figure \ref{fig:Schematic_BVP2_Scenario1}.
