\end{figure}
%
    \item Scenario 2: Two steps are considered in this scenario. In the first step, damage, $d$, is ramped linearly from 0 to 0.45 over 100 seconds along the left and top surfaces of the rectangle while it is fixed. In the second step, a displacement boundary condition is applied to its right ($u_1$) and bottom surfaces ($u_2$) simultaneously, ramped linearly from 0 to 0.05 mm over 200 seconds, while the applied damage, $d$, applied in the first step is held constant throughout the entire step, as seen in Figure \ref{fig:Schematic_BVP2_Scenario2}.
%
