The cones were assembled in the manner as follows. First, the PEEK housing is machined from a $2$-inch cube, and the bases of each of the six cones are affixed to the housing. Next, the tips of the three fixed cones are adhered to the curved surface of the halfball lens. They are configured in such a way that the halfball lens' apex is centered in between the cones to allow for maximum light throughput.

